----------------------------------
   -- Plus 3.0.2 - 10/16/2026 --

- the desktop app now comes as a zip like the original editor: unzip it anywhere and run
  'Sound Space Quantum Editor Plus.exe'
- the app updates itself: when a new version is out it asks, downloads it and restarts into it
  (turn this off with SETTINGS > OTHER > Check For Updates)
- playtesting in Rhythia is back in the desktop app: SETTINGS > PLAYER > Rhythia, choose RHYTHIA PATH, then PLAYTEST
- fixed the video not showing when exporting to NOVASTRA (NPK) in the desktop app
- sharper desktop icon

IF YOU HAVE 3.0.1: download this version's zip by hand once; updates are automatic from then on

----------------------------------
   -- Plus 3.0 - 10/16/2026 --

Sound Space Quantum Editor is now SOUND SPACE QUANTUM EDITOR PLUS!

- new name and logo
- a desktop app for Windows: every update is published on GitHub releases (installer or portable .exe)
- the desktop app shows what you're doing on Discord, and tells you when a new version is out
- quick animations when moving between menus; opening a map now shows that it's loading instead of freezing
- export/import your whole setup as one .ssqes file (SETTINGS > EXPORT SETUP / IMPORT SETUP): editor and map player
  settings, keybinds, custom background, grid cursor and note mesh, and optionally what the auto mapper and bot learned
  (in the desktop app, double-click a .ssqes to import it)

AUTO MAPPER (PATTERNS tab):
- learns from every map you open, and from many at once with LEARN FROM MAPS
- finds the song's BPM and its downbeats, and maps on the beat; streams stay perfectly even
- finds drops, build-ups and changes inside a drop, and changes the pattern with the music; drum fills get a burst
- maps only where the song makes sounds (choose what to sync to: kicks, snares, hi-hats, melody, bass); quiet parts
  stay empty and there are no random cuts where the music carries on
- difficulty 1-10 (10 is properly hard), density, an exact number of notes, quantum on/off, and more in MORE OPTIONS
- copies the design of the maps you give it (one map's style at a time, even with 200 learned), never copies
  impossible parts and keeps every move playable
- doesn't freeze the editor while it works

EDITOR:
- grid zoom and note size sliders
- custom grid cursor image (animated GIFs too), editor background image, custom .obj note meshes on the grid
- MAP PLAYER button in the menu
- RHM export, and fixes for SSPM export

MAP PLAYER:
- 3D backgrounds, custom note meshes, uncapped FPS and an option to turn off background effects
- realistic autoplay that learns how you play from your replays

